 days […], weeks […] moons […]; but also into ritual and farming cycles. This created the need for specialists who, from observing the heavenly bodies and the seasons, would declare the beginning and the end of each moon or cycle or year. This, in Igbo, was known as Igu Afo (counting the year) and was very important since it was tied to the very survival of the community.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2363, 'temperature': 0.2})
